   "notes": "This is a thermal EOS, not a standalone room-temperature Vinet fit. Equations 1 and 4-8 add a Debye Mie-Gruneisen pressure increment relative to 300 K; with a=1, gamma(V)=gamma0*(V/V0)^b and theta(V)=theta0*exp[-gamma0*((V/V0)^b-1)/b]. The paper also reports an equally successful BM3-MGD alternative: V0=46.55 A^3 fixed, K0=294(2) GPa, K0'=4.85(12), theta0=1130(100) K, gamma0=1.66(7), a=1 fixed, and b=2.9(4). Vinet is retained as the single executable record from this paper because Figure 2 uses it and Tables 3-4 present its values first, with BM3 in parentheses; the authors state that the two fits agree within analytical uncertainty rather than explicitly designating a preferred model. The fixed V0 rounds the independently measured recovered-sample value 46.553(19) A^3; null in parameter_errors means it was not a fitted coefficient, not that the ambient measurement lacked uncertainty. Several measurements crossed the established stishovite-CaCl2-type boundary without transforming on the experimental timescale; the authors report that excluding them gives identical fit results, so the marginal P-T envelope is not a rectangular phase-stability claim.",
